You should check your process limits, using ulimit -a. This will show
you the virtual memory limit for your process. ulimit -Ha will show
you the maximum hard limits. You can increase your process limits upto
the hard limits. More than this and you will need to use dxkerneltuner
to increase the system limits.

If you want to see how much memory your machine has use vmstat -P, if
you want to see how much swap then use swapon -s.

Big.H


