My 13-year-old son just installed Redhat 7.1 on an AlphaServer 4100,
surely you can't be having that much trouble, heh heh heh...

I did have to help him puzzle out one problem, maybe it's the one that
bit you: if you follow the instructions for a boot command at the SRM
prompt, it kernel panics.  We finally decided maybe it was dropping
everything on the command line after it wrapped at 80 columns (even
though SRM is happy to parse it, even going so far as to prompt him to
continue when he forgot the closing double-quotes!)  The workaround was
to actually set the boot_osflags parameter to what it needed to be for
the CD install, which allowed him to avoid typing the -flags and its
parameters on the boot line, which brought it under 80 characters.

(Just to keep this on-topic for the newsgroup, I'm of course running
hobbyist VMS on the other AlphaServer 4100!)

Duncan


