While Kingston offers only 128MB DIMM's for the au series, their PC133
ECC SDRAM Value ram, while not certified for the au, works perfectly.
I am using 4 of these DIMM's each in a 433au and a 600au together with
the two 64MB DIMM's which were in the systems when we bought them. 

Kingston's part number is KVR133X72C3/256 for a single 256MB DIMM
and I bought 10 for 37$ a piece (8 for the two Alphas and another
two for a Sun Blade 100).

I initially only bought two DIMMS to try if they would work in the au.
They worked but what I noticed when I got the other 8 was that while
the first two used chips made by Infinion, the other 8 used chips
made by NEC. Looks like Kingston uses whatever is cheapest for their
Value ram series. Both types worked fine though.

