The system can support up to 1.5GB with the use of 256MB DIMMs in pairs.
Crucial and Kingston only offer 128MB DIMMs in their lines, so the max using
_only_ DIMMs from either vendor would be 768MB.  My PWS600au has 1GB made up
of the original pair of DEC 256MB DIMMs (huge buggers) and two pairs of
Crucial 128MB DIMMs.  Works perfectly, but I'd have to replace the Crucials
to upgrade past the current amount; I probably won't need to though.

Rich Jordan





