That's [configuration changing without service interruption]
what we were working towards with TOPS-10 SMP.  One of the
bugaboos of the -10 monitor structure was having device
drivers and data hardcoded into the resident monitor.  To 
put in a second controller (or a new controller) required
a reload of the monitor if it hadn't been built with expansion
in mind.  But we never got time to work on it.

