advscan does not hurt nor delete anything
mkfset will create a new fileset in a domain and will throw an eror
message if the fileset exists. So normally does not hurt either.

The only damageable command is
mkfdmn which will erase all your previous domain on the partition you
run that command.

advscan was the *good* way to recover, actually it only creates the
domain_rz0g in /etc/fdmns, and write the sym link to the partition in
there :

You're confused with domain and filesets :

Domain name is the name of the directory in /etc/fdmns. This directory
contains a sym link to the device[s](partition[s]) containing the
domain structure and data.
Within a domain, you can have several filesets (which are similar to
filesystems) sharing the pool of bytes of the domain.

The filesets names are in the structure of the domain. The only way to
catch their names is

# showfsets domain_name

Then, when you know their names use:
# mount domain_name#fileset_name /mnt

and not mount domain_name#partition or whatever.

