cjt & trefoil <cheljuba@prodigy.net> writes:

> I thought the Itanium was in some sense compatible with PA-RISC.  Doesn't 
> that make "compatiblity and porting issues" a near no-brainer?

The IA64 ISA shows quite some PA-RISC heritage, and HP has made sure that they
can translate PA-RISC code to IA64 code in an efficient and performant way (as
such things go). Nonetheless, the low level stuff in an OS needs to be adapted
to the new hardware. And there is the problem that with HP-UX being big-endian,
a HP-UX system on IA64 will be mixed-endian (little-endian code, big-endian
data), which takes some care in compilers and tools to get right.

	Jan


