HP-Compaq a windfall for 2 banks
Bloomberg Business News

NEW YORK -- Goldman Sachs Group and Salomon Smith Barney may earn more
than $30 million each for advising Hewlett-Packard Co. and Compaq
Computer Corp. on their merger this week, based on industry averages.

The two banks weren't hired until July, more than a year after
Hewlett-Packard's chief executive, Carly Fiorina, and her Compaq
counterpart, Michael Capellas, started talking and one month after
details of the merger began to be worked out.

The investment banks used their top executives to seal the transaction.

Investment banks often bring merger ideas to a client or provide advice
on the best way to complete a transaction. In this case, most of that
work was already done.




