Hello folks:

Good news! I resolved problems with console terminal tests on test #3...
However, it failed to boot with ?4 message during test #3.  I looked
into that debug log file.  I learned that firmware want to test parity
check.  On my screen:

KA630-A.V1.3

   7..6..5..4..3..
?4
Failure.

When it set up MSER<2> (Write Wrong Parity), then put a trap on desired
location to try to read.  When it attempts to read, Machine-Check 
exception occured with parity error settings on MSER and CEAR register.

MOVB #03,@#MSER          <- Enable wrong parity write
MOVL #55555555,@#FF0000  <- Put a trap on location FF0000.
MOVB #01,@#MSER          <- Turn off it.
MOVL @#FF0000,R5         <- Machine-Check Exception occurs.

Does anyone know parity check alogrithm?  I believe that parity check
slows down my emulation or so.

Thank you!

-- Tim Stark

