Franco Tassone wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
> in order to improve performances I've just upgraded the memory of my mVaxII,
> as I substituted a m7608 4mb board (in row 3) with a m7609 8mb board, and so
> I
> obtained 12mb of ram, here you can see the resulting layout of
> the adapters:
> 
>    +---
>  Q |  1 ka630 ------------+
>  / |  2 m7608 (4 mb) -----+
> CD |  3 m7609 (8 mb) -----+
>    |  4 m7516 (deqna adap.)
>    +---
>  Q |  5 m3107 - m7546 (serial + tk50 adap.)
>  / |  6 m7555 (rd53 adap.)
>  Q .
>    .
> 
> Now I'm trying to obtain 16mb of memory by reinstalling the m7608 were it
> was originally, that is in row 3, to install m7609 in row 4 and shifting by
> one place all the remaining adapters. I re-builded the "scsi-like" connector
> in order to link the one more memody module to the cpu module, and connected
> them
> This is the result:
> 
>    +---
>  Q |  1 ka630 -----------+
>  / |  2 m7608 (4 mb) ----+
> CD |  3 m7608 (4 mb) ----+
>    |  4 m7609 (8 mb) ----+
>    +---
>    |  5 m7516 (deqna adap.)
>  Q |  6 m3107 - m7546 (serial + tk50 adap.)
>  / |  7 m7555 (rd53 adap.)
>  Q .
>    .
> The system gives no life signs when I connect the third memory module, it
> boots normally when I disconnect it from the "scsi-like" flat.
> 
> Is it possible such a memory configuration on a mvaxII ?
> Thanks in advance.


A MicroVAX II (KA630) can only use 2 memory modules.  The "SCSI-like"
cable is a PMI (Private Memory Interconnect?) cable.  The correct one
for a MicroVAX II has 3 connectors.  The 4 connector one is used on a
MicroVAX III (KA650).

To get 16MB on a MicroVAX II, you need (2) 8MB boards.

BTW: With a 8MB and 4MB board, you should have seen 13MB of memory.  The
KA630 board has 1MB.  With 2 8MB boards, the extra 1MB is ignored.

