The DECbrouter (aka 'DISCO') is DEC hardware (made compatible with
the CISCO 2500 or IGS [68030 processor]) and CISCO software (IOS).

AFAIK The last official software for the DECbrouter was 11.1.6 and
included IP,IPX,XNS,DECnet,LAT, ... protocols. I think CISCO called
this feature set the 'enterprise version' then.

I see no reason (except the RAM/EPROM requirements of newer IOS versions)
why the normal CISCO software for the 2500 series router won't run
on the DECbrouter. Though I still haven't tried it myself.
Better start with the 'IP only' version of the CISCO IOS to avoid a
RAM/EPROM upgrade of the DECbrouter hardware as long as possible.

Good luck (and post answers here)

