Hello folks (or Jeff):

Good news! I implemented some and fixed some bugs.  I encountered a 
few big problems during test #4, etc.  In test #4, I learned and had 
implemented the prefetch instruction buffer.  It will not work
without the prefetch instruction buffer.  When it turned memory 
management on, next instruction crashed.  When it was done, a page
is not affected until any branch instruction that cause the prefetch
instruction flush.  Also it resulted much faster!  On 450 Mhz Pentium III, 
it is estimated VUP 1.3.

Test was counted down to 3.  During test #7, I got welcome messsage and 
starting 7 to count down on my screen.  During test #3,  it crashed.   I 
looked into my debug log file and found out that some "undocumented" 
information in console terminal registers.  It is waiting for RXCS<11> bit 
forever.  That is not docemented in my VAX reference handbook, etc.  I 
believe that it is one of KA630's implementations.  Primary boot (console 
program) almost was finished before OpenVMS boot started (secondary 
boot ater >>> prompt).  When test #3 is passed, >>> prompt will be 
printed.  Test #2 to #0 are secondary boot for OpenVMS.

Does anyone have complete console terminal registers for KA630 processor
(MicroVAX II)?

Thank you!

-- Tim Stark

