> believe that it is one of KA630's implementations.  Primary boot (console
> program) almost was finished before OpenVMS boot started (secondary
> boot ater >>> prompt).  When test #3 is passed, >>> prompt will be
> printed.  Test #2 to #0 are secondary boot for OpenVMS.
> 
> Does anyone have complete console terminal registers for KA630 processor
> (MicroVAX II)?

Here's the layout for the Console Receive Control Status Register:

   <31:12>             unused, read as zeros

   <11:11>  RCV ACT  - Receive Active. This read-only bit is set at
                       the center of the start bit of the serial input
                       data, and is cleared at the expected center
                       (per DLART timing) of the stop bit at the end of
                       the serial data. RX DONE is set one bit time
                       after RCV ACT clears.

   <10:08>             unused, read as zeros

   <07:07>  RX  DONE - Receiver Done. This read-only bit is set when
                       an entire character has been received and is
                       ready to be read from the RBUF register. This
                       bit is automatically cleared when RBUF is
                       read. It is also cleared by power-up, by the
                       negation of DC OK, and by writes to the BIR.

   <06:06>  RX  IE   - Receiver Interrupt Enable. This R/W bit is
                       cleared by power-up, by the negation of DC
                       OK, and by writes to the BIR. If RX DONE and
                       RX IE are both set, a program interrupt is
                       requested.

   <05:00>             unused, read as zeros

Given the description of RCV ACT, I am surprised that the firmware
would be looking for it, since it will go away as soon as the stop bit
for the current character is half received. Since RX DONE will then
set one bit time later why bother?

Here's the Console Receiver Data Buffer Register layout:

   <31:16>            unused, read as zeros

   <15:15>  ERR     - Error. This read-only bit is set if RBUF bit 14
                      or 13 is set. ERR is clear if these 2 bits are
                      clear. This bit cannot generate a program
interrupt.

   <14:14>  OVR ERR - Overrun Error. This read-only bit is set if a
                      previously received character was not read
                      before being overwritten by the present character.

   <13:13>  FRM ERR - Framing Error. This read-only bit is set if the
                      present character has no valid stop bit.

   <12:12>            unused, read as zero

   <11:11>  RCV BRK - Receive Break. This read-only bit is set at the
                      end of a received character for which the serial
                      data input remained in the SPACE condition for all
                      eleven bit times. RCV BRK the remains set until
                      the serial data input returns to the MARK
                      condition. RCV BRK is also cleared by power-up
                      and by the negation of DC OK.

   <10:08>            unused, read as zero

   <07:00>            Received Data Bits. These read-only bits
                      contain the last received character.

> 
