The Console Transmitter Control Status Register is laid out:

   <31:08>              unused, read as zeros

   <07:07>   TX  RDY  - Transmitter Ready. This read-only bit is clear
                        when the XBUF is loaded and sets when the
                        XBUF can send another character. XMT RDY is
                        set by power-up, negation of DC OK, and by
                        writes to the BIR.

   <06:06>   TX  IE   - Transmitter Interrupt Enable. This R/W bit is
                        cleared by power-up, negation of DC OK, and by
                        writes to the BIR. If both TX RDY and TX IE are
                        set, a program interrupt is requested.

   <05:03>              unused, read as zeros

   <02:02>   MAINT    - Maintenance. This R/W bit is used to facilitate
                        a maintenance self-test. When MAINT is set, the
                        external serial input is disconnected and the
                        serial output is used as the serial input.
                        This bit is cleared by power-up, negation of
                        DC OK, and by writes to the BIR.

   <01:01>              unused, read as zero

   <00:00>   XMIT BRK - Transmit Break. When this R/W bit is set, the
                        serial output is forced to the SPACE condition.
                        XMIT BRK is cleared by power-up, negation of
                        DC OK, and by writes to the BIR.


The Console Transmitter Data Buffer Register is laid out as:

   <31:08>              unused

   <07:00>              transmit character bits.

The TXDB is a write-only register.

Jeff


