A monopoly is defined in legal terms as a proportion of market share, 
whether there are alternatives is _completely_ immaterial. US vs IBM
was successful (i.e. it obtained the consent decree), despite the fact
that IBM had plenty of competition in the form of the seven dwarves.
The point of monopoly legislation is to prevent companies with a very
large market share from using the power generated by that market share
to their unfair advantage.

