Hewlett-Packard, Compaq Continue Falling on Purchase Concerns
By Peter J. Brennan

Palo Alto, California, Sept. 5 (Bloomberg) -- Hewlett-Packard Co. and Compaq
Computer Corp. shares fell for the second straight day since the companies
announced plans to combine, on concern that rivals will benefit during the
transition.

Hewlett Packard fell $1.27, or 6.7 percent, to $17.60 in midafternoon trading.
